# Containerfile.inc — rename to exactly `Containerfile.inc` to activate.
#
# Use this ONLY for something the declared fields cannot express: an extra
# builder stage, a second layer, or an ARG with a default. A build secret or
# a build arg is NOT a reason — declare `secret` and `arg` in module.kdl and
# the generator writes the mounts for you.
#
# The generator inlines this file VERBATIM alongside the standard block, so
# it ADDS to the normal flow rather than replacing it: the module still gets
# its usual layer, with its mounts, its options and its flavor gate.
# Shipping the file is the whole declaration; module.kdl only says where it
# goes, and only when the defaults are wrong:
#
#   fragment position="after"        # "before", above the block, is default
#   fragment standard-layer=#false   # emit nothing but this file
#
# With `standard-layer #false` the fragment is the only thing this module
# emits, so it has to call run-module.sh itself and mount everything that
# needs. Nothing then carries a `secret`, `arg`, `option` or collected file,
# so declaring any of those alongside it is a lint error.
#
# One module in the repository ships one: kernel/cachyos-kernel, for its
# `ARG KERNEL=cachyos`, which is graph shape rather than a parameter and is
# the line the kernel-freshness workflow rewrites. Its build arg and signing
# secret are declared in its manifest, not written out here.
#
# A fragment is emitted unconditionally, so on a flavor-gated module
# anything it RUNs has to set FLAVOR_GATE itself; the generator cross-checks
# that against the flavor block the module is listed in.
#
# Example skeleton (a full override, which is rarely what you want):
#
# RUN --mount=type=bind,from=ctx,source=/modules/GROUP/template,target=/ctx/modules/GROUP/template \
#     --mount=type=bind,from=ctx,source=/lib,target=/ctx/lib \
#     --mount=type=cache,target=/var/cache \
#     --mount=type=cache,target=/var/log \
#     --mount=type=tmpfs,target=/tmp \
#     --mount=type=secret,id=example_secret,target=/run/secrets/example,required=false \
#     bash /ctx/lib/run-module.sh /ctx/modules/GROUP/template
